{"archetypes":[{"name":"ci-gate","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff changes a head-bound GitHub required-check registration gate before admin merge.","prompt_body":"Investigate whether the two-phase CI gate correctly distinguishes registration timeout from required-check failure. Check that required checks count as registered only for the pushed head SHA and that stale PR head state cannot allow a merge. Verify that timeout paths skip the watch phase while successful registration proceeds to watch and then admin merge. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"shell-contract","focus_area":"code-quality","weight":1,"rationale":"The changed shell scripts have strict stdout and set-e contracts that are easy to regress.","prompt_body":"Review the shell control flow for unsafe set -e interactions, command substitutions that may abort unexpectedly, and helper calls whose failures should be captured rather than propagated. Pay special attention to jq probes, KEY=value stdout hygiene, stderr redaction, and sleep fallback behavior. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"gh-harness","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The regression coverage relies on a complex PATH-injected gh stub with branch and head-OID simulation.","prompt_body":"Examine the test harness stubs for GitHub CLI behavior and ensure they faithfully model the production paths being tested. Check the split between registration JSON probes and watch invocations, default head OID derivation, mismatch knobs, probe counters, and no-op sleep wiring. Look for cases where the harness could pass while production behavior remains broken or where existing scenarios are accidentally changed. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"publish-tail","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"Re-enabling the design run-log flush changes the end-of-design lifecycle sequencing and failure propagation.","prompt_body":"Trace the design publish tail from plan write through marker, diagram upsert, run-log publish, final summary render, issue rename, and cleanup gating. Verify that publish failure metadata is preserved, final summaries still render when appropriate, and rename or cleanup cannot run after failed publish envelopes. Compare the script behavior with the documented lifecycle expectations. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"admin-merge","focus_area":"security","weight":1,"rationale":"The change intentionally uses admin merge after CI gating, so bypass boundaries and diagnostics need focused review.","prompt_body":"Assess whether the admin merge path remains fail-closed and does not become an unconditional branch-protection bypass. Check that stale checks, missing checks, failed checks, and head mismatch leave the PR open with safe diagnostics and PUBLISH_OK=false. Also verify that captured GitHub output is redacted before surfacing across public or persisted artifacts. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
